  "result": "No actions this turn. I've already read the repo and have what I need to ask the first question.\n\n---\n\nI looked through the app. The timetable page is built from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, and the site has no warnings yet. So the real gap is getting the news of a cancellation to the site, not showing it.\n\nMany cancellations happen on the day, because of weather or a breakdown. A nightly file would miss those until the next morning. How the news reaches the site decides most of what we build: who enters it, how quickly it appears, and whether the office's export has to change.\n\n**When a sailing gets cancelled today, who decides it, and how does word get out to staff and passengers?**",
